Node ID=900 order inquisition exposer
Text=The Inquisition came out of the siege with the most intact command structure left in Barcelona, and the city handed it the rebuilding. Part of that standing was your doing. You walked into the Temple District and told them where La Calle Perdida was, and your directions were good, because you had been inside it as a friend. The Holy Office took the quarter apart over nine days and spent thirty years cataloguing what it found there. The men who did the work were promoted on the strength of your word, the pyres were lit in the plaza where the markets had been, and the cities paid for the wood.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order inquisition killer
Text=The Inquisition came out of the siege with the most intact command structure left in Barcelona, and the city handed it the rebuilding. You had worn its mark and you had killed its own, and the Holy Office is an organisation that keeps careful records of a name entered twice. Its fires burned on through the peace exactly as they had burned through the war, because a frightened city asks its inquisitors for more work rather than less, and the cities paid for the wood without being asked twice. Nothing was ever formally charged against you. But there were four towns between Barcelona and the coast that you never entered again, and you knew all four names.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
