Node ID=900 order horde
Text=The goblin tribes came down out of the mountains, counted themselves, and found that they were many, and that nothing in the west was counting at all. You had been a chum of the Horde, which in their mouths means useful rather than trusted, and they kept the word for as long as any of them remembered you. A Khan's banner rose again inside three generations. The border towns burned first, and the chronicles of the west recorded it as a surprise. Two trade paths through the mountains stayed open that entire time, and nobody ever wrote down why.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
