Node ID=900 order savage heart betrayed
Text=The Savage Heart came out of the war the way mercenary companies do, which is richer and with a shorter roster, and one of the names on the short side was Raylark's. You took his contract, and then you took the Khan's, and you carried the Everlasting into Khara'Khorum to prove you had earned it. The company does not avenge its dead, it prices them, and the price it set on you was entered in the books at Marseilles and never once collected. In the years after Alamut the Savage Heart turned away more work than it could staff. None of it was ever yours, and that was the whole of its revenge.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order savage heart
Text=The Savage Heart came out of the war the way mercenary companies do, which is richer and with a shorter roster. You took Raylark's contract and killed goblins for the bounty, counted by the ear, and the company's books still carry the entry under your name. In the years after Alamut half of Europe wanted men who would do that sort of work and not ask after the paperwork, and the Savage Heart raised its rate twice in five years. Raylark kept his camp west of Khara'Khorum until he was too old to hold it. The Horde had learned to count western killers by name, and yours was one of the names.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
